  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Making a GOGO-Loco style group of submenus/settings default in the quick actions menu a default thing on every avatar.\n\nThis would include: The default VRC animation; different sit, stand, and laying positions; and position locking (locking you in place by your hip/root-bone).\n\nIt’s almost unheard of now for creators to not put gogo on an avatar, as it’s a MASSIVE accessibility feature for:\n\n- Quest users that can’t get/use OVR and don't have full body.\n\n- PC players that don’t have full-body\n\n- AND ESPESHALLY desktop players! Since without it, they just have to crouch with friends in a mirror, looking unnatural/silly just crawling on the floor with friends, but with it it allows them to sit normally and naturally with their in vr friends.\n\nAnd it is SOOO useful to those that have drift, affecting ALLL headsets that use joycons on their controllers, both PC and standalone headsets! Since being able to lock yourself in place stops you from having to use your big menu to keep you still (which means you can't use the expressions wheel/toggles), or having to use the emoji wheel to keep your drift at bay, making you spew random unintentional emojis.... All this just to chat with friends and not be drifted away.\n\nI feel it’s a must-have these days, which is why it’s rare to see public, or P2U avis without it! Having it implemented would mean, (just like scaling) It can be used on almost every avi, including older ones uploaded before GOGO was even made!",
